Goal
Fix a functional bug where Rule W8001 (unused condition) is incorrectly reported when a condition is applied to resources generated by AWS::LanguageExtensions Fn::ForEach, specifically when an inner collection depends on an outer identifier (e.g., Fn::FindInMap keyed by an outer Fn::ForEach variable). The root cause is that the transform does not propagate the current foreach params into collection resolution consistently, and there is a parameter order bug at a critical call site. Implement the smallest, backward-compatible fix and validate it with targeted tests.
Important constraints
- Do not broaden the scope beyond this bug. Do not modify rule logic (W8001) or any time-based rule behavior. Ignore unrelated failing tests (e.g., Quickstart integrations, E2533).
- Keep API changes backward-compatible.
- Do not add new “success_templates” or unrelated tests. If you create temporary tests or files for reproduction, delete them before finishing.
- Do not commit; we will commit later.
What to implement
Thread the current Fn::ForEach params context through collection evaluation and fix the argument order at the call site so that nested collections can resolve values that depend on outer identifiers.
Concretely:
- Ensure _ForEachCollection.values has the signature:
  def values(self, cfn, collection_cache, params=None)
  and internally uses params when resolving collections (e.g., FindInMap that references the outer identifier).
  This signature must remain backward-compatible with existing call sites (params is optional).
- Ensure _ForEach.items passes params to the collection.values call in the correct order:
  items = self._collection.values(cfn, self._collection_cache, params)
  The previous failed attempt passed arguments in the wrong order, which caused params to be mistaken for the cache dict.
- Ensure _Transform._walk calls foreach.items(cfn, params) so the params flow is preserved across nested foreach expansions.
- Search for all other .values( ... ) call sites and verify they pass arguments in the order (cfn, collection_cache, params). Do not change the meaning of existing arguments anywhere else.
Step-by-step plan
1) Read and understand the issue
- The false positive arises because nested Fn::ForEach collections, such as Fn::FindInMap keyed by an outer loop variable, evaluate without knowing the current outer params. The current code fell back to generating placeholder values instead of the correct items, so the resource that should reference Condition ShouldCreateBucket3 was never generated, and W8001 reported it as unused.
